    "Paths": {
      "universal": {
        "name": "Universal",
        "description": "A universal path, skills with this path can be selected if it has roles matching thosee of your paths"
      },
      "barbarian": "A barbarian is a fierce, untamed warrior who channels raw emotion and primal fury into devastating combat prowess, thriving where instinct matters more than discipline.",
      "fenceroflostbriarith": "A fighting style that relies on specialised weapon techniques and swapping between stances.",
      "divineadherent": "You worship a deity and derive your powers from prayer and devotion to that deity.",
      "poisoner": "Adept at the production and the usage of poisons.",
      "shieldedfighter": "A shielded fighter blends offense and defense, using weapon and shield in perfect balance.",
      "shieldguardian": "A selfless fighting style, one where you put yourself in harm's way to shield your allies and prevent your enemies from reaching them.",
      "snake": "A style employing the use of two short weapons and relies on rapid speed and dodges.",
      "sniper": "Snipers are the unseen predators of the battlefield, patiently waiting for the moment to strike. They excel in precision shooting, taking down high-value targets, and keeping their location hidden even after an attack. In addition to their deadly aim, Snipers can gather information from afar, guiding their allies with vital intel.",
      "sorcerer": "A magician that draws on internal powers to manifest spells."
    },
    "Archetypes": {
      "ranger": "Masters of the wild and patient hunters, Rangers live for the open air and the satisfaction of a well-placed shot. Whether stalking prey through dense forest or shadowing an enemy force from a ridgeline, Rangers are built for striking from afar and surviving in hostile terrain. In a party, Rangers excel at reconnaissance, harrying enemies from distance, and controlling the battlefield’s range. Their craft blends precision marksmanship with tactical movement — keeping foes off-balance and allies well-informed."
    },
